SUMMARY:Deadline: Andrew Carnegie Fellows Program 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Andrew Carnegie Fellows Program awards USD 200\,000 each to
  scholars\, journalists\, authors and public intellectuals for one to two 
 years of research and writing toward a book or major study in the social s
 ciences and humanities\, with recent classes framed around understanding U
 S political polarization and strengthening social cohesion.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Carnegie Corporation of New York\nLocation: US. For US-based scholars\,
  journalists\, authors and public intellectuals\; candidates must be nomin
 ated by their institution (direct applications are not accepted).\nAward: 
 USD 200\,000 over one to two years for research and writing toward a book 
 or major study. NOTE: institutional nomination required\; individuals cann
 ot apply directly.\nDuration: One to two years of funded research and writ
 ing.\n\nMore: https://carnegie.org/our-work/special-projects/andrew-carneg
 ie-fellows/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://carnegie.org/our-work/special-projects/andrew-carnegie-fellows/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:US. For US-based scholars\, journalists\, authors and public intel
 lectuals\; candidates must be nominated by their institution (direct appli
 cations are not accepted).
END:VEVENT
